From e7c1e89e3dfeaea1bc7a12e88b04293baa0c711f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 14:14:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(editor): heading outline rail

Adds a quiet "On this page" rail on the right edge of wide editor
canvases (>=1100px, >=3 H1-H3 headings). It reuses the navigator TOC's
Markdown heading source and scrollToNoteHeading jump logic, debounced
150ms, and highlights the heading in view via rAF-coalesced scroll
tracking. Clicking also places the caret in the heading. On wide
canvases the rail replaces the popover TOC launcher; it fades with
writing focus. Adds a persisted "Toggle Outline" palette command.
